   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to certain portions\nof the New York state thruway where maximum dimension and weight limitations\nof vehicle shall not be applicable",
    "basePrintNo": "S7818",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7818-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §385, V & T L (as proposed in S.6332-A & A.7417-A)",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7818\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to certain\nportions of the New York state thruway where maximum dimension and\nweight limitations of vehicle shall not be applicable\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo make a technical amendment to a chapter authorizing tandem trucks to\nuse a portion of the road past Thruway Exit 25-A.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one makes a technical amendment to clarify that tandem trucks\nwould still be authorized to use a tandem lot access road that was\npreviously authorized in statute prior to the underlying chapter.\n\nSection two of this bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe chapter amendment makes a technical change to clarify that tandem\ntrucks can still use a tandem lot access road that was authorized in the\noriginally enacted statute.\n\nThe conversion to cashless tolling eliminates the ability of double\ntandem trucks to utilize Exit 25-A for inbound distribution. Vehicles\npassing through the exit at higher rates of speed in both directions\nrender truckers unable to access the parking lot directly adjacent to\nExit 25-A, which is where they have traditionally unhooked the second\ntrailer of the tandem in order to comply with the VTL rules prohibiting\ntandem trucks from traversing the surrounding roads. This scenario would\nlead to double tandem trucks to utilize alternative routes in order to\nget their freight to distribution centers, meaning even longer driving\ntime for double tandem trucks on local roads.  Additionally, longer\ndriving times would negatively impact the environment by way of\nincreased emissions.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021: Underlying chapter passed Senate 63-0 (S.6332-A) and passed Assem-\nbly 148-0.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, in the same manner as S.6332-A.\n",
